<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Sabilla</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1929</span> · Also known as Battle of Sibilla · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ikhwan-revolt">Ikhwan revolt</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Sabilla was fought on 29 March 1929 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/najd">Najd</a>, central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>, between the forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-saud">Ibn Saud</a> and the Ikhwan, the tribal religious warriors who had helped him conquer Arabia but rebelled against his ban on raiding into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> and Kuwait and his acceptance of modern innovations. Ibn Saud's victory broke the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ikhwan-revolt">Ikhwan revolt</a>, which was finally crushed early in 1930.</p></div>
